Oh,  I see there are two approaches:
1. Hayes and Preacher (2014) estimate the relative indirect effects.  a1 is the difference in intercepts between experimental 1 and control group; a2 is the difference in intercepts between experimental 2 and control group.
I found a conflicting result: 1) a1, a2, and b differ from zero (there is mediation), but 2) a1b=0 and a2b=0 (no mediation).
https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24188158/

2. multiple-group approach estimates group differences in indirect effect.
Are the two approaches similar?

